            "review_title": "Review at Cello Xua Cafe & Cuisine",
            "review_text": "Philip B\nNha Trang, Vietnam4 contributions\n0\nDon't bother\nMar 2017\nWent tonight ordered fried rice with garlic and pork chop with fries in a mushroom sauce. Pork came out was very small,3 pieces of pork and a small amount of fries. To be fair was nice (a bit fatty) but no where near enough. I had finished eating but still no fried rice/garlic for my partner. When enquired still no response. Partner had enough by now and decided to get the bill. After what seemed like a lifetime partner goes over to the waiter for the bill and he asked if she wanted her food to take away. As you can imagine she was not impressed. Waiter did apologise to me but no one would speak to her. With my meal no knife and no napkins, overall not a great experience. If your considering going don't bother there are plenty of really good restaurants around the corner. Eg yens, ganesh, olivier to name a few.\nRead more\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten March 5, 2017",
